        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto">FF149 adds support for <code class="notranslate">HTMLElement.captureStream()</code> in <a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2017708" rel="nofollow">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2017708</a> - and this was recoreded in <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="3995050060" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29135" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29135/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29135">#29135</a>.</p>
<p dir="auto">Previously only a non-standards-compliant version <code class="notranslate">mozCaptureSttream()</code> was defined. The docs contained notes about the compliance issues. This attempts to move those to BCD, where they belong.</p>
<p dir="auto">Related work for this can be tracked in <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="3978086146" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43215" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/43215/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43215">mdn/content#43215</a></p>]]></content>
