        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Update compatibility data for `api.AudioParam.cancelScheduledValues`]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29150</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29150"/>
        <updated>2026-03-03T15:46:25.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/68780890?u=ead4e493844141826b3007c4bbf730edd1df630a&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><h4 dir="auto">Summary</h4>
<p dir="auto">Updates <code class="notranslate">api.AudioParam.cancelScheduledValues</code> to mark partial support for older Chrome/Safari versions and Firefox.</p>
<h4 dir="auto">Test results and supporting details</h4>
<p dir="auto">Per the March 2020 spec update (<a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="501625877" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/WebAudio/web-audio-api/issues/2071" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/WebAudio/web-audio-api/issues/2071/hovercard" href="https://github.com/WebAudio/web-audio-api/issues/2071">WebAudio/web-audio-api#2071</a>), <code class="notranslate">cancelScheduledValues</code> should cancel in-progress curve events created by <code class="notranslate">setValueCurveAtTime</code>. Chrome and Safari have implemented this behavior, but Firefox has not.</p>
<p dir="auto">Supported by the following implementation evidence and release notes:</p>
<p dir="auto"><strong>Chrome</strong>:</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>Chromium bug: <a href="https://crbug.com/1063502" rel="nofollow">Bug 1063502</a></li>
<li>Implementation: <a href="https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/7a87148abe74349f55729acfbd54ebb02418aac6" rel="nofollow">Commit 7a87148a</a></li>
<li>Release: <a href="https://chromiumdash.appspot.com/commits?commit=7a87148abe74349f55729acfbd54ebb02418aac6&amp;platform=Windows" rel="nofollow">Chrome 83</a></li>
</ul>
<p dir="auto"><strong>Safari</strong>:</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>WebKit bug: <a href="https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=216132" rel="nofollow">Bug 216132</a></li>
<li>Implementation: <a href="https://trac.webkit.org/changeset/266558" rel="nofollow">Changeset r266558</a></li>
<li>Release: <a href="https://webkit.org/blog/11300/release-notes-for-safari-technology-preview-114/" rel="nofollow">Safari TP 114</a>, <a href="https://webkit.org/blog/11648/new-webkit-features-in-safari-14-1/" rel="nofollow">Safari 14.1</a></li>
</ul>
<p dir="auto"><strong>Firefox</strong>:</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>Not implemented (<a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1752775" rel="nofollow">Bug 1752775</a>)</li>
</ul>
<h4 dir="auto">Related issues</h4>
<p dir="auto"><span class="issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se" aria-label="This pull request closes issue #29029.">Fixes</span> <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="3931073911" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29029" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29029/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29029">#29029</a></p>]]></content>
